  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q23-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "23",
    "prompt": "Find the value(s) of $p$ so that the line $y=px-4$ will touch the parabola $y=x^2-4x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$p=0$ or $p=-8$.",
      "worked": "At an intersection, the two expressions for $y$ are equal.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-4x&=px-4\\\\x^2-(p+4)x+4&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor tangency, the intersection quadratic must have a repeated root, so $\\Delta=0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(p+4)^2-16&=0\\\\(p+4)^2&=16\\\\p+4&=\\pm4\\\\p&=0\\text{ or }-8\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 33
  },
